-- =====================================================================
-- Session 145 — Matt 15 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 15''s extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2), S132 (Matt 3), S133 (Matt 4),
-- S134 (Matt 5), S135 (Matt 6), S137 (Matt 7-8 paired), S138 (Matt 9),
-- S139 (Matt 10), S140 (Matt 11), S142 (Matt 12), S143 (Matt 13), and
-- S144 (Matt 14) extras-tier coverage. Single chapter migration — Matt
-- 15 is the Pharisaic-Yerushalayim-delegation-controversy chapter, with
-- the chapter''s four framework-major moments landing in (a) the
-- Pharisaic-Corban-evasion-of-the-fifth-commandment (vv.1-9 — the
-- *making the commandment of Elohim (God) of none effect by your
-- tradition* declaration and the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 29:13 *teaching for
-- doctrines the commandments of men* citation locking the framework''s
-- diagnostic-substance for the modern-Judaizer-movement reading); (b)
-- the heart-defilement-versus-mouth-defilement teaching (vv.10-20 — the
-- Pharisaic-fence-architecture''s inversion of the Torah''s defilement-
-- substance dismantled and the heart-Torah of Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah)
-- 31:33 / Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27 restored, WITHOUT abolishing
-- the Torah''s clean-and-unclean architecture of Vayikra (Leviticus) 11);
-- (c) the Canaanite-woman pericope at Tsor (Tyre) and Tsidon (Sidon)
-- territory (vv.21-28 — the King''s-most-direct-mission-scope statement
-- *I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Yashar''el
-- (Israel)* at v.24, and the woman''s-faith-honored within the
-- architecture rather than overruling it, with the seed-distinction of
-- Red Line #7 preserved); (d) the Galilee-mountain-healings and the
-- feeding-of-the-four-thousand (vv.29-39 — with the seven-baskets-of-
-- the-second-feeding paired with the twelve-baskets-of-the-feeding-of-
-- the-five-thousand at Matt 14:20 encoding the framework''s eschato-
-- logical-arc, twelve-tribes-gathered into Yovel-restoration-completion
-- per Vayikra (Leviticus) 25:8-10 and Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 61:1-2''s
-- *acceptable year of Yahuah (the LORD)*). The short.md walks the
-- Yovel-completion substance against the inherited-Christian-categorical-
-- Gentile-feeding misreading.
--
-- Matt 15 reading-target: the chapter walks four narrative-movements
-- with the Tanakh-substance carrying the heaviest framework-bearing
-- anchors directly (Shemot (Exodus) 20:12 + 21:17 for the fifth-
-- commandment substance the Corban-tradition violates; Yeshayahu
-- (Isaiah) 29:13 for the *commandments of men* diagnostic-citation;
-- Bereshit (Genesis) 6:5 + Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 17:9 + Yechezk''el
-- (Ezekiel) 36:26-27 for the heart-substance the King restores; Matt
-- 10:5-6 + Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 34:11-16 + Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 50:6
-- for the lost-sheep-mission-scope at v.24; 1 Melakhim (Kings) 17:8-24
-- for the widow-of-Tsarephath Tanakh-precedent for the Canaanite-woman
-- pericope; Vayikra (Leviticus) 25:8-10 + Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 61:1-2 for
-- the Yovel-substance the seven-baskets signal). The extras-library
-- adds five framework-bearing thread-clusters: Sirach (Ecclesiasticus)
-- 3 + 7 + Tobit 4 on the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the
-- fifth-commandment substance the Pharisaic-Corban-tradition voids
-- (Thread 1); Sirach 15:11-20 + 27 + Wisdom of Solomon 1:11 on the
-- heart-as-the-source-of-evil-and-the-Father-NOT-being-the-source
-- substance the King restores at the heart-defilement teaching (Thread
-- 2); Sirach 36:1-17 + 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 13:40-48 + Tobit 13:5 on the
-- direct wisdom-stream-articulation of the gathering-of-the-scattered-
-- twelve-tribes prayer-and-prophecy substance the King''s-lost-sheep-
-- mission-scope at v.24 enacts (Thread 3 — FRAMEWORK-MAJOR); Jubilees
-- 15:30-32 + 16:17 + 22:11-12 on the seed-of-promise-specifically-to-
-- Yashar''el-and-not-to-the-other-seed-of-Avraham (Abraham) substance
-- (the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the seed-distinction the
-- Canaanite-woman pericope honors at the children''s-bread-vs-dogs''-
-- crumbs metaphor — Thread 4 — FRAMEWORK-MAJOR); Jubilees 50:1-4 on
-- the Yovel-cycle architecture (the year-weeks-and-the-jubilees-from-
-- Adam framework Jubilees structures the entire Tanakh-chronology
-- around — Thread 5 — the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Yovel-
-- substance the seven-baskets-of-the-second-feeding signal). 1 Enoch
-- does not surface framework-bearing Matt 15 connections at S145 (the
-- Apocalypse-of-Weeks at 1 Enoch 91-93 was not parsed into verse-
-- granularity in the local corpus; the watchers-substance does not
-- bear on Matt 15''s Pharisaic-controversy or mission-scope-lock).
-- Sonnini''s Acts of Paul, Ascension of Isaiah, Apocalypse of Abraham,
-- Adam-Eve Conflict, and Jasher do not surface framework-bearing Matt
-- 15 connections at S145. Historical-witness editions (Josephus, M.R.
-- James''s apocryphal NT, Lightfoot''s Apostolic Fathers) remain
-- deferred from V1 cross-refs per the historical-witness one-way rule.
-- The lookup view retains the full S139 edition set for forward
-- compatibility.
--
-- Five PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1. `honor-of-parents-fifth-commandment-the-corban-tradition-voids-in-sirach-and-tobit`  (sort 297)
--   2. `the-heart-the-source-of-evil-not-the-father-in-sirach-and-wisdom-of-solomon`        (sort 298)
--   3. `gathering-of-the-scattered-twelve-tribes-in-sirach-and-2-esdras-and-tobit`          (sort 299)
--   4. `seed-of-promise-specifically-to-yasharel-not-other-seed-of-avraham-in-jubilees`     (sort 300)
--   5. `yovel-cycle-and-the-year-weeks-architecture-in-jubilees`                            (sort 301)
--
-- 20 new cross_references rows at tier_required=''extras'' (Library tier,
-- $4.99) + 5 new cross_reference_threads at tier_required=''complete_study''
-- (Companion tier, $9.99). The tier split honors the two-layer
-- architecture of the chapter-end card: Layer 1 (per-verse cross-refs)
-- visible to Library readers who have access to the extras-library
-- editions the refs point to; Layer 2 (framework thread callouts with
-- summary_md + member_notes) gated at Companion, since the threads ARE
-- the framework''s reading of how canon and library answer each other —
-- the "hidden detail expand" that is the Companion-tier upgrade. Every
-- member-note passes the 12 Red Lines and the 12-point editorial
-- checklist. Hebrew names with internal apostrophes (Yashar''el,
-- Ya''aqov, Yechezk''el, Yo''el, Sha''ul, Mikha''el, Gavri''el,
-- Shemu''el, Mosheh''s, King''s, Father''s, Yahuah''s, Yochanan''s, etc.)
-- are escaped per SQL single-quoted-string-literal convention (every
-- internal ' doubled to '').
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on every INSERT.
-- =====================================================================

\echo 'Session 145 — Matt 15 extras-tier cross-references migration starting...'
BEGIN;

-- Verse-lookup temp view. Mirrors the S144 view including
-- `sonnini-acts-29`; retained for forward compatibility even though
-- Matt 15 does not surface a Sonnini Acts 29 connection at S145.
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s145_verse_lookup AS
SELECT
    e.slug AS edition_slug,
    b.slug AS book_slug,
    c.chapter_number,
    v.verse_number,
    v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v
  JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id
  JOIN books    b ON c.book_id    = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN (
       'canon',
       'enoch',
       'jubilees',
       'jasher',
       'apocrypha',
       'apocrypha-charles-vol1',
       'pseudepigrapha',
       'adam-eve-conflict',
       'apocalypse-of-abraham',
       'ascension-isaiah',
       'sonnini-acts-29'
   );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 20 extras-tier cross_references rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH input(src_edition, src_slug, src_ch, src_v,
           tgt_edition, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES

  -- Thread 1: honor-of-parents-fifth-commandment-the-corban-tradition-voids-in-sirach-and-tobit
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 4, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 3, 1,
   '*Hear me your father, O children, and do thereafter, that you may be safe.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 3:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the fifth-commandment substance — the parental-honor architecture the Torah commands at Shemot (Exodus) 20:12. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:4''s *honour thy father and mother* citation. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the parental-honor-substance as the foundation-of-the-children''s-safety; the Pharisaic-Corban-tradition the King exposes at vv.3-6 voids the architecture at the support-of-the-aged-parent level. The wisdom-stream''s articulation reinforces the Torah-substance the King defends against the Pharisaic-tradition; the same architecture, the same load-bearing covenant-substance, the same diagnostic of the Pharisaic-system that voids the parental-honor commandment through the Corban-vow-mechanism.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 4, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 3, 8,
   '*Honour your father and mother both in word and deed, that a blessing may come upon you from them.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 3:8 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the holistic-parental-honor substance — both in word and deed. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:4-6''s King''s-charge that the Pharisaic-Corban-tradition voids the parental-honor commandment. The Corban-tradition allowed the son to claim parental-honor-in-word (the formal-religious-vow appeared honorable) while voiding it in deed (the actual support-of-the-aged-parent was blocked by the vow''s legal-mechanism). The wisdom-stream had named the architecture: honor must be BOTH word AND deed. The Pharisaic-Corban-tradition split them and called the word-without-the-deed righteous. The King names the split and dismantles it.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 4, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 7, 27,
   '*Honour your father with your whole heart, and forget not the sorrows of your mother.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 7:27 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the whole-heart-parental-honor substance with the specific-remembering-of-the-mother''s-sorrows. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:4''s parental-honor commandment and the Pharisaic-Corban-evasion of vv.5-6. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture at the heart-level — honor your father with your WHOLE HEART; the Pharisaic-Corban-tradition violated the architecture by establishing a divided-heart-allowed-by-the-vow-mechanism. The King''s-restoration of the heart-substance at vv.18-20 will close the loop on the heart-level the wisdom-stream had named.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 6, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 3, 16,
   '*He that forsaketh his father is as a blasphemer; and he that angereth his mother is cursed: of Yahuah (God).* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 3:16 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the forsaking-the-father-as-blasphemy substance — the framework''s reading of the Pharisaic-Corban-tradition at the worst-end of its diagnostic. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:6''s *thus have ye made the commandment of Elohim (God) of none effect by your tradition.* The Pharisaic-Corban-tradition that allows the son to forsake the support-of-the-aged-parent is — at the wisdom-stream''s articulation — the disposition of blasphemy and curse. The King''s-charge at v.6 lands at the same load-bearing diagnostic the wisdom-stream had named: the disposition that voids the parental-honor commandment is at the architecture of blasphemy-against-the-Torah-the-Father-spoke-from-Sinai. The Pharisaic-system''s-righteousness-credentialing was at the architecture the wisdom-stream had named cursed.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 4, 'apocrypha', 'tobit', 4, 3,
   '*And when he had called him, he said, My son, when I am dead, bury me; and despise not your mother, but honour her all the days of your life, and do that which shall please her, and grieve her not.* Tobit 4:3 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the deathbed-instruction-of-the-Tobit-father to-his-son on the parental-honor architecture extending-to-the-mother-all-the-days-of-her-life. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:4''s parental-honor commandment. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture across the second-Temple-Yashar''el (Israel) household-life: the parental-honor extends to the holistic-care of the mother (and by implication the father) across the entire-duration of the parent''s-life. The Pharisaic-Corban-tradition the King exposes at vv.5-6 voids exactly this architecture; the wisdom-stream had named the substance the tradition was voiding centuries before.'),

  -- Thread 2: the-heart-the-source-of-evil-not-the-father-in-sirach-and-wisdom-of-solomon
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 11, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 15, 11,
   '*Say not you, It is through Yahuah (God) that I fell away: for you oughtest not to do the things that he hates.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 15:11 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Father-NOT-being-the-source-of-the-man''s-falling-away substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:11''s *not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the mouth, this defileth a man.* The King is restoring the substance-of-defilement to the heart-and-mouth (intentions, words, deeds proceeding from-the-heart) — the substance the wisdom-stream had named centuries before. The Father is NOT the source of the man''s-defilement (Sirach 15:11''s articulation); the man''s-own-heart IS the source (Matt 15:18-19''s articulation). The two articulations cohere at the heart-and-mouth-substance-as-the-locus-of-defilement architecture; the rabbinic-fence-tradition that had located-defilement at the un-washed-hands-and-the-food-categorically-touched-by-them inverted the architecture the wisdom-stream and the Torah had named.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 18, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 15, 20,
   '*He has commanded no man to do wickedly, neither has he given any man licence to sin.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 15:20 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Father-NOT-commanding-wickedness and the Father-NOT-giving-licence-to-sin substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:18-19''s *those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they defile the man. For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture: the Father has not commanded-wickedness and has not given-licence-to-sin; therefore the source-of-the-wickedness-and-the-sin is NOT-the-Father; therefore the source IS the man''s-own-heart-out-of-which-the-evil-thoughts-and-the-second-table-Decalogue-violations-proceed. The King''s-articulation at Matt 15:18-19 lands the substance the wisdom-stream had named at the gospel-level''s precision.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 18, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 27, 6,
   '*The fruit declareth if the tree have been dressed; so is the utterance of a conceit in the heart of man.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 27:6 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the tree-and-fruit-and-utterance architecture — the heart''s-conceit manifests in the utterance-of-the-mouth. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:18''s *those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture in the tree-and-fruit-metaphor centuries before; the King''s Matt 7:17-20 *every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth evil fruit* operates in the same architecture; the King''s Matt 15:18 articulation locks the operative-form: the heart''s-substance manifests in the mouth''s-utterance and the deeds-that-follow. The cause-and-effect-of-hearing diagnostic per Red Line #11 carries through the same architecture — the heart''s-substance determines what the mouth-and-deeds reveal.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 19, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 1, 11,
   '*Therefore beware of murmuring, which is unprofitable; and refrain your tongue from backbiting: for there is no word so secret, that shall go for nought: and the mouth that belieth slayeth the soul.* Wisdom of Solomon 1:11 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the mouth-and-tongue substance — the murmuring, the backbiting, the lying-mouth all operate at the soul-slaying register. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:19''s catalogue: *evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies.* The Wisdom of Solomon catalogue (murmuring, backbiting, the lying-mouth) and the King''s catalogue (false witness, blasphemies) overlap at the mouth-substance level. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture; the King names the operative-form. The framework reads this in continuity with the broader-Tanakh-substance: the tongue-and-the-mouth are the manifest-substance of the heart-Torah of Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 31:33 / Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27 that the King is restoring.'),

  -- Thread 3: gathering-of-the-scattered-twelve-tribes-in-sirach-and-2-esdras-and-tobit
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 24, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 36, 1,
   '*Have mercy upon us, O Yahuah (God) of all, and behold us.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 36:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the gathering-of-the-scattered-tribes prayer — the petition-for-mercy on the scattered-people-of-the-covenant. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:24''s *I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Yashar''el (Israel).* The wisdom-stream''s prayer-for-the-gathering operates as the petition the King''s-mission answers at the gospel-level: the lost-sheep-of-the-house-of-Yashar''el (Israel) are the recipients-of-the-mercy the Sirach 36 prayer petitioned-for. The framework reads the lost-sheep-mission-scope at v.24 as the King''s-answer to the wisdom-stream''s-articulated-petition for the gathering of the scattered-tribes.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 24, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 36, 11,
   '*Gather all the tribes of Jacob together, and inherit you them, as from the beginning.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 36:11 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the gathering-of-all-the-tribes-of-Ya''aqov (Jacob) substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:24''s lost-sheep-mission-scope. The wisdom-stream''s prayer is for the gathering-of-ALL-the-tribes-of-Ya''aqov (Jacob) — the explicit articulation of the twelve-tribes-restoration-substance the prophets had named (Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 37:21; Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 31:8-10; Hosea 1:10-11; Zekharyah (Zechariah) 10:6-10). The King''s-mission-scope at v.24 IS the operative-form of the wisdom-stream''s-prayer at Sirach 36:11; the lost-sheep-of-the-house-of-Yashar''el (Israel) the King is sent-to IS the all-the-tribes-of-Ya''aqov (Jacob) the wisdom-stream had prayed for the gathering of. The framework reads this as FRAMEWORK-MAJOR for the lost-sheep-mission-scope''s wisdom-stream confirmation.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 24, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 13, 40,
   '*Those are the ten tribes, which were carried away prisoners out of their own land in the time of Osea the king, whom Salmanasar the king of Assyria led away captive, and he carried them over the waters, and so came they into another land.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 13:40 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the ten-tribes-carried-away-by-the-Assyrian-exile substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:24''s lost-sheep-mission-scope. The lost-sheep-of-the-house-of-Yashar''el (Israel) the King''s-mission addresses at v.24 are precisely the ten-tribes 2 Esdras 13:40 names — the scattered-northern-house-of-Yashar''el (Israel) the Assyrian-deportation carried-into-the-territories-of-the-dispersion. The framework reads this in continuity with the broader-Tanakh-substance of the Assyrian-exile (2 Melakhim (Kings) 17:6, 17:23; 1 Divrei HaYamim (Chronicles) 5:26) and the prophetic-gathering-architecture (Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 37 + 47; Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 31).'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 24, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 13, 48,
   '*But those that be left behind of your people are they that are found within my borders.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 13:48 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the remnant-found-within-the-borders substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:24''s lost-sheep-mission-scope. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the remnant-and-the-scattered-tribes-coming-home; the King''s-mission addresses both registers — the remnant-within-the-borders (the Galilee-and-Yahudah multitudes) AND the scattered-tribes-in-the-territories-of-the-dispersion (the broader-mission the apostolic-extension will reach). The framework reads the lost-sheep-mission-scope at v.24 as encompassing both registers the wisdom-stream had named.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 24, 'apocrypha', 'tobit', 13, 5,
   '*And he will scourge us for our iniquities, and will have mercy again, and will gather us out of all nations, among whom he has scattered us.* Tobit 13:5 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the scourge-then-mercy-then-gathering-out-of-all-nations substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:24''s lost-sheep-mission-scope. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the gathering-out-of-all-nations-among-whom-the-Father-had-scattered-the-people — the exact-architecture the prophets had named (Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 37:21''s *I will take the children of Yashar''el (Israel) from among the heathen, whither they be gone, and will gather them on every side*) and the King''s-mission enacts at v.24. The framework reads the Tobit 13:5 substance in continuity with the broader-Tanakh-substance and the King''s-mission-scope at Matt 15:24.'),

  -- Thread 4: seed-of-promise-specifically-to-yasharel-not-other-seed-of-avraham-in-jubilees
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 22, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 15, 30,
   '*For Ishmael and his sons and his brothers and Esau, Yahuah (God) did not cause to approach Him, and he chose them not because they are the children of Abraham, because He knew them, but He chose Yashar''el (Israel) to be His people.* Jubilees 15:30 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the seed-of-promise-specifically-to-Yashar''el (Israel)-NOT-to-other-seed-of-Avraham (Abraham) substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:22-28''s Canaanite-woman pericope. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture: Avraham (Abraham) had many descendants (Yishma''el (Ishmael), Esav (Esau), and others); the covenant-seed-of-promise is SPECIFICALLY-Yashar''el (Israel), NOT the broader-Avrahamic-genealogy. The King''s-distinction at vv.26-27 (children-of-the-house vs the dogs-under-the-table) operates in the architecture the wisdom-stream had named: the covenant-seed has a specific-identity that is not collapsed-into-broader-Avrahamic-genealogy or into-categorical-nations-inclusion. The framework reads this as FRAMEWORK-MAJOR for the Red Line #7 seed-distinction''s wisdom-stream confirmation. The Canaanite-woman is outside the seed-architecture the wisdom-stream had named with explicit-precision.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 26, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 15, 31,
   '*And He sanctified it, and gathered it from amongst all the children of men; for there are many nations and many peoples, and all are His, and over all has He placed spirits in authority to lead them astray from Him.* Jubilees 15:31 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the seed-distinction architecture: the many-nations-and-many-peoples are under spirits-in-authority placed by the Father; Yashar''el (Israel) is sanctified-and-gathered-from-amongst-all-the-children-of-men. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:26''s *it is not meet to take the children''s bread, and to cast it to dogs.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the spiritual-jurisdictions over the nations (the *bene Elohim* allocation per Devarim (Deuteronomy) 32:8-9 in the Septuagint and Dead Sea Scrolls reading); the King''s-distinction at v.26 operates in the same architecture: the children-of-the-house are the sanctified-Yashar''el (Israel) under the Father''s-direct-rule; the dogs-under-the-table are the categorical-nations under the spiritual-authority-architecture the Father had placed at the dispersion-of-Babel.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 26, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 15, 32,
   '*But over Yashar''el (Israel) He did not appoint any angel or spirit, for He alone is their ruler, and He will preserve them and require them at the hand of His angels and His spirits.* Jubilees 15:32 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Yashar''el (Israel)-under-Yahuah''s-direct-rule architecture. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:24-26''s lost-sheep-mission-scope and children-vs-dogs distinction. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture: Yashar''el (Israel) alone is under the direct-rule of the Father; the King''s-mission-at-v.24 to the lost-sheep-of-the-house-of-Yashar''el (Israel) operates in the architecture of the Father''s-own-direct-shepherding-of-the-scattered-flock (Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 34:11-16). The Canaanite-woman is outside the Yashar''el (Israel)-under-direct-rule-architecture the wisdom-stream had named; the mercy-at-the-crumbs-substance the King grants at v.28 operates within-the-architecture (as the master''s-table-mercy to the dogs-under-the-table) without collapsing the architecture''s-distinction.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 26, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 16, 17,
   '*And (that) all the seed of his sons should be nations, and be reckoned with the nations; but from the sons of Isaac one should become a holy seed, and should not be reckoned among the nations. For he should become the portion of Yahuah (God) most High.* Jubilees 16:17 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the seed-of-promise-specifically-to-Yitschaq (Isaac)-NOT-to-other-sons-of-Avraham (Abraham) substance, with the explicit-precision that the holy-seed should-not-be-reckoned-among-the-nations. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:26''s children-vs-dogs distinction. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture: the holy-seed from the sons-of-Yitschaq (Isaac) is the portion-of-Yahuah-most-High and is NOT-reckoned-among-the-nations; the other-seed-of-Avraham (Yishma''el (Ishmael), the sons of Keturah at Bereshit (Genesis) 25:1-4, and the Esav (Esau)-line through Yitschaq''s (Isaac''s)-non-elect-son) are reckoned-with-the-nations. The King''s-distinction at v.26 operates exactly in the architecture the wisdom-stream had named at Jubilees 16:17. The framework reads this in continuity with Romans 9:6-13''s *they are not all Yashar''el (Israel), which are of Yashar''el (Israel) ... in Yitschaq (Isaac) shall thy seed be called* — Paul''s articulation of the same Tanakh-and-extras-library substance.'),

  -- Thread 5: yovel-cycle-and-the-year-weeks-architecture-in-jubilees
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 37, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 50, 1,
   '*And after this law I made known to you the days of the Sabbaths in the desert of Sinai, which is between Elim and Sinai.* Jubilees 50:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Sabbath-architecture revealed-in-the-desert-of-Sinai substance — the architecture Jubilees structures the entire-Tanakh-chronology around. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:37-38''s seven-baskets-remaining and the short.md''s reading of the seven-architecture as the Yovel-cycle-completion substance. The wisdom-stream of Jubilees had structured the Tanakh-chronology around the Sabbath-of-years and the Yovel-cycle architecture; the King''s-seven-baskets at Matt 15:37 signal the completion-substance the Jubilees-framework had named the architecture for.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 37, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 50, 2,
   '*And I told you of the Sabbaths of the land on Mount Sinai, and I told you of the jubilee years in the sabbaths of years.* Jubilees 50:2 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the jubilee-years-in-the-sabbaths-of-years architecture — the seven-times-seven-years-equals-forty-nine-years-then-the-fiftieth-year-jubilee substance of Vayikra (Leviticus) 25:8-10 the wisdom-stream of Jubilees had named the chronological-architecture for. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:37''s seven-baskets-remaining. The seven-architecture of the second-feeding signals the Yovel-completion-substance the Jubilees-wisdom-stream had structured the entire-Tanakh-chronology around. The King''s-pedagogical-double-feeding (twelve-baskets at Matt 14:20 for the twelve-tribes-gathering; seven-baskets at Matt 15:37 for the Yovel-completion) encodes the architecture''s-completion-arc the wisdom-stream had named the chronological-substance for.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 15, 37, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 50, 4,
   '*Wherefore I have ordained for you the year-weeks and the years and the jubilees: there are forty-nine jubilees from the days of Adam until this day, and one week and two years.* Jubilees 50:4 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the forty-nine-jubilees-from-Adam-until-this-day architecture — the framework''s-chronological-substance Jubilees had structured the entire-Tanakh-history around at the Yovel-cycle level. The framework reads the verse against Matt 15:37''s seven-baskets-remaining. The Jubilees-wisdom-stream had counted the architecture''s-completion-arc from-Adam-forward at the Yovel-cycle level; the King''s-seven-baskets at Matt 15:37 signal the same architecture''s-completion-substance reached at the gospel-pivot. The framework reads this in continuity with Luke 4:18-21''s Natsareth (Nazareth)-synagogue-reading of Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 61:1-2''s *acceptable year of Yahuah (the LORD)* — the King''s-naming-himself as the One the Yovel-substance-proclaims at the gospel-fulfillment.')

)
INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, 'extras'::content_tier
  FROM input i
  JOIN _s145_verse_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug = i.src_edition
                            AND sv.book_slug    = i.src_slug
                            AND sv.chapter_number = i.src_ch
                            AND sv.verse_number  = i.src_v
  JOIN _s145_verse_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug = i.tgt_edition
                            AND tv.book_slug    = i.tgt_slug
                            AND tv.chapter_number = i.tgt_ch
                            AND tv.verse_number  = i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

